   "title": "In Study 1, the probability of choosing the lottery rose with the lottery's expected-value advantage over the safe option (t(4796) = 9.26, p < 3.1e-20, β = 0.074).",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Participants took the lottery more often the better it was, showing their choices were sensible. — Anchor: “participants’ probability of choosing the risky option (lottery) increased with the difference between the expected value of the lottery and the value of the safe option”"
   },
   "sourceDocument": "https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.105391.2",
